WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.200
A hunt plan records the hypothesis, rationale, scope, time range, assets, data sources, expected behavior, reviewers, safety constraints, and completion criteria.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:17.226
This structure makes the work repeatable and prevents the investigation from expanding without purpose.

00:00:17.226 --> 00:00:22.893
Preserve evidence references, searches, observations, and decisions as the hunt progresses.

00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:31.279
Findings should distinguish facts from interpretation and assign a confidence level based on coverage and source quality.

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:37.853
Record disconfirming evidence and unresolved gaps, not only observations that fit the theory.

00:00:37.853 --> 00:00:43.972
Escalation paths should identify security, operations, engineering, site leadership, and incident-response contacts.

00:00:43.972 --> 00:00:50.092
High-consequence findings may require rapid coordination, but response authority should remain clear.

00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:54.852
Documentation helps teams act without improvising around sensitive systems.

00:00:54.852 --> 00:00:56.892
Operationalize repeatable findings.

00:00:56.892 --> 00:01:03.012
A reliable pattern may become a detection, dashboard, watchlist, or recurring review.

00:01:03.012 --> 00:01:13.212
Document required fields, thresholds, exclusions, asset context, investigation steps, and ownership so the output can be maintained after the original hunt.

00:01:13.212 --> 00:01:16.158
Hunts also improve foundational data.

00:01:16.158 --> 00:01:21.372
Update asset inventory when new systems or dependencies are validated.

00:01:21.372 --> 00:01:32.025
Record blind spots, repair collection gaps, improve time and identity mapping, and add process or maintenance enrichment that made the hunt possible.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:39.958
Close each hunt with the result, confidence, affected assets, evidence, operational explanation, actions, and follow-up owner.

00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:46.078
Measure value through decisions and improvements, not the number of searches performed.

00:01:46.078 --> 00:01:53.104
A well-documented inconclusive hunt can still reveal exactly what visibility the program needs next.
